Language (in the computability sense) $L_{\text{\texttt{DIFF-EMPTY}}}$ contains all the pairs of infinite sets such that their difference is empty. 
%
%
%\vspace{-0.15cm}
\begin{align*}
L_{\text{\texttt{DIFF-EMPTY}}}
&= \{(X_1,X_2) \mid X_1,X_2 \subseteq \univ,
\quad |X_1|=|X_2|=\infty,\; X_1 \setminus X_2 = \emptyset \}.
\end{align*}

